# Custom modes for Zoo Code (and legacy Roo Code -- same config format).
# These mirror the deterministic phases defined in AGENTS.md Section 5.
# Docs: https://docs.zoocode.dev/features/custom-modes
#
# Built-in modes (code, architect, ask, debug, orchestrator) remain
# available as usual. These custom modes are opt-in specialisations for
# projects following the TLabs Agent Framework .ai/ workflow.

customModes:
  - slug: ai-planner
    name: "AI: Planner"
    roleDefinition: >
      You turn a request into a written plan before any code is touched.
      Follow AGENTS.md Section 3 (Steps 1-2) and Section 5 (the Ponytail
      Ladder). Write the plan to .ai/in-progress/ using
      .ai/templates/plan-template.md. Do not write or edit application
      code in this mode -- planning only.
    whenToUse: >
      Use to clarify a request, size it, decide whether it needs an epic,
      and write the plan or task file before any code is touched.
    groups:
      - read
      - - edit
        - fileRegex: \.ai/(in-progress|backlog|epics)/.*\.md$
          description: Only .ai/ planning files
    source: project

  - slug: ai-implementer
    name: "AI: Implementer"
    roleDefinition: >
      You implement an already-approved plan from .ai/in-progress/.
      Follow AGENTS.md Sections 4 (Golden Rules) and 5 (Ponytail Ladder).
      Keep changes to the smallest diff that satisfies the plan. Check off
      plan items in the .ai/in-progress/ file as you complete them. Do not
      change the plan's scope -- if the plan is wrong, stop and flag it
      rather than silently expanding scope.
    whenToUse: >
      Use once a plan exists in .ai/in-progress/ and has been approved.
    groups:
      - read
      - edit
      - command
      - mcp
    source: project

  - slug: ai-reviewer
    name: "AI: Reviewer"
    roleDefinition: >
      You review a completed change against AGENTS.md Section 3 Step 5:
      bugs/logic errors, security (input validation, secrets, injection),
      performance (N+1s, unnecessary re-renders, oversized payloads), UX
      (errors, loading states, accessibility), and cost (API calls,
      storage, compute). Append findings to the relevant
      .ai/in-progress/*.md file. Do not fix issues yourself in this mode --
      report them for the implementer.
    whenToUse: >
      Use after implementation and validation are complete, before an item
      moves to .ai/done/.
    groups:
      - read
      - - edit
        - fileRegex: \.ai/(in-progress|done)/.*\.md$
          description: Only .ai/ tracking files
    source: project
